          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.147
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Net of a sphere? Experiment and see if you can make a paper cutout that can perfectly wrap around a ball without leaving any wrinkles, gaps or overlaps."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.166,
            0.456,
            0.187
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Shortest Paths on a Cube"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.197,
            0.847,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider an interesting problem related to the discussion so far. We know that on a plane, the shortest path between two points is the straight line between them. Now, what is the shortest path between two points on the surface of a cuboid, if we are allowed to travel only along its surface?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.289,
            0.846,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": "Let us imagine a hungry ant living on the surface of a cuboid. To its good fortune, there is a laddu on the surface."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.418,
            0.337,
            0.688,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "**Laddu** (at the centre of the top face)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.56,
            0.412,
            0.814,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": "**Ant** (at the centre of the side face)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.511,
            0.698,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "？ What is the shortest path for the ant to reach the laddu?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.547,
            0.488,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": "？ What about in the following case?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.813,
            0.492,
            0.903,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.576,
            0.688,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.439,
            0.597,
            0.685,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": "**Laddu** (at the centre of the edge)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.746,
            0.847,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": "？ If we think that a certain path is the shortest, how can we be sure that it truly is, among all the infinite possibilities?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.792,
            0.644,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": "For example, are either of these the shortest path?"
        },
